<title>USA: British Aerospace to sell $600 mln in yankee debt.</title>
<headline>British Aerospace to sell $600 mln in yankee debt.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>British Aerospace Plc is expected to sell at least $600 million in 10-year and 30-year bonds in the U.S. later this week, market sources said.</p>
<p>J.P. Morgan Securities will be the lead manager of the 144A private placement offering of yankee bonds, which are rated A3/A-minus.</p>
<p>The size of the individual tranches has not been determined, the sources said. Price talk was not yet available.</p>
<p>((-U.S. Corporate Bond Unit, 212-859-1662))</p>
</text>
